Lyna,

Selecting the appropriate analysis is based on a combination of the hypothesis one wishes to test, and the data types they have. A careful reading of the help file will assist for part of this, and will point to some of the primary literature.

You post mentioned that you have a single factor, location. Thus I can divine that you wish to compare disparities among locations? One option (again, as per the help file) is to estimate partial disparities following Foote. That is found as #4 of the options you listed (see help file).  Another option is to account for location in the linear model.

Good luck,

Dean

